CODEGEN.md §5.12: a getter of an input field called before LoadInputs signals E8302 at run
time; the generated C++ getter calls canon::OnEvalError with the registry's rendered text
(internal/gen/cpp's e8302 renders it from the template; TestE8302MatchesFindingsTxtar checks the getter).
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Config: one input field.
public record Config {
  /// apiKey, from the environment.
  apiKey: input String(1..)? from env "A_API_KEY"
}

let config: Config = Config {}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a" }
-- findings.txt --
E8302: a.Config.apiKey is a runtime input and LoadInputs has not been called
